            "met"
          ],
          "event": "Severe Thunderstorm Warning",
          "urgency": "immediate",
          "severity": "severe",
          "certainty": "observed",
          "expires": "2026-09-07T00:15:00-06:00",
          "headline": "Severe Thunderstorm Warning issued September 6 at 11:28PM MDT until September 7 at 12:15AM MDT by NWS Great Falls MT",
          "description": "SVRTFX\n\nThe National Weather Service in Great Falls has issued a\n\n* Severe Thunderstorm Warning for...\nNortheastern Fergus County in central Montana...\n\n* Until 1215 AM MDT.\n\n* At 1128 PM MDT, a severe thunderstorm was located 19 miles\nnortheast of Roy, or 25 miles south of Zortman, moving northeast at\n35 mph.\n\nHAZARD...Half dollar size hail.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Damage to vehicles is expected.\n\n* This severe thunderstorm will remain over mainly rural areas of\nnortheastern Fergus County.",
          "instruction": "For your protection move to an interior room on the lowest floor of a\nbuilding.\n\nTorrential rainfall is occurring with this storm, and may lead to\nflash flooding. Do not drive your vehicle through flooded roadways.",
          "effective": "2026-09-06T23:28:00-06:00",
          "onset": "2026-09-06T23:28:00-06:00",
          "senderName": "NWS Great Falls MT",
          "responseType": [
            "shelter"
          ],
          "web": "http://www.weather.gov"
        }
      ],
