      "alertInfo": [
        {
          "@type": "AlertInfo",
          "inLanguage": "en-US",
          "category": [
            "met"
          ],
          "event": "Flood Advisory",
          "urgency": "expected",
          "severity": "minor",
          "certainty": "likely",
          "expires": "2026-09-07T01:30:00-06:00",
          "headline": "Flood Advisory issued September 6 at 11:23PM MDT until September 7 at 1:30AM MDT by NWS Denver CO",
          "description": "* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is expected.\n\n* WHERE...Northeastern Larimer County in north central Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 130 AM MDT.\n\n* IMPACTS...Minor flooding in low-lying and poor drainage areas.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n\n- At 1123 PM MDT, Doppler radar indicated heavy rain due to\nthunderstorms. Minor flooding is ongoing or expected to begin\nshortly in the advisory area. Between 1.25 and 1.75 inches of\nrain have fallen.\n\n- This includes the following streams and drainages...\nSand Creek, Spottlewood Creek, Rawhide Creek, Spring Creek,\nRabbit Creek, Park Creek, Coal Creek, Boxelder Creek, North Fork\nCache La Poudre River, Lonetree Creek, Lone Pine Creek and Dry\nCreek. Additional rainfall amounts of 0.5 to 1 inch are expected\nover the area. This additional rain will result in minor\nflooding.\n\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nLivermore, Buckeye and Owl Canyon.",
          "instruction": "Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nBe especially cautious at night when it is harder to recognize the\ndangers of flooding.",
          "effective": "2026-09-06T23:23:00-06:00",
          "onset": "2026-09-06T23:23:00-06:00",
          "senderName": "NWS Denver CO",
          "responseType": [
            "avoid"
          ],
          "web": "http://www.weather.gov"
        }
      ],
      "area": [
